abstract: >-
  Reproducible code, pre-registration protocol, deviation log, and derived
  datasets for a two-phase study of Inka khipus across OKR v2.1.0 (n = 611)
  and disjoint KFG-only Excel workbooks (n = 36). Phase 1 reports pre-registered
  inter-archive invariance controlling for column count and sample size, explicit
  tabular outlier accounting (21/86), and a null result (0/30 BH-FDR) against
  five highland Textos Andinos schemas calibrated with power and proxy controls.
  Phase 2 (exploratory) documents five candidate hierarchical regularities of
  subsidiary cords (including a vertical spacing dose-response contrast and
  blind KFG out-of-sample replication), regional archive variation across eight
  sites, and a corpus-wide 611 x 611 rare-number sweep surfacing a putative
  three-khipu Berlin split-ledger link (VA 42518 <-> VA 63038 b / VA 63038(B))
  and an unflagged reversed physical duplicate (VA 24370(B) <-> VA 66834).
